course: dictionary
lesson: 9409
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context, the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer means. «The squash ball hit the back wall with a loud smack.» The ball and the wall point to the sport, so squash means the racket game here.
explain: «Please squash the empty cans before you put them in the recycling.» Squash here is an action, not a game or a drink. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence? Press flat fits, so that is the meaning. Try it: «Please press flat the empty cans» sounds odd, but the meaning is clear.
explain: Look at the grammar too. «The squash was crowded» and «it's a squash» are different from «a squash grew in the garden». When squash is a noun, it can be a vegetable or a sport, and when it is a verb, it is an action. Read the whole sentence before you decide what the word means.
fact: Squash is a verb (to press something flat or squeeze it into a small space) and a noun (a vegetable, a sport or a drink).
fact: «Squashed» can mean crushed flat or out of shape, as in «a squashed sandwich».
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, squash is a sweet drink made by adding water to concentrate, such as «orange squash».
fact: A squash is also a vegetable that grows on a vine, such as butternut squash, courgette or pumpkin.
fact: In science, a squashed can has the same mass but a different shape, because squashing changes the shape, not the amount of material.
exercise: «The children squashed the empty cans before the recycling bin was emptied.» What does squashed mean here? | *Pressed flat | Thrown far away | Filled with water | Painted bright red
exercise: «We squashed into the lift with eight other people.» What does squashed mean? | Lost a game | Pulled out of the way | *Squeezed into a small space | Ran very fast
exercise: Priya asks for orange squash at the picnic. What is orange squash? | *A sweet drink made by adding water to concentrate | A small rubber ball | A vegetable that grows on a vine | A wooden bat for hitting a ball
test: «The butternut squash grew all summer on the vine in the garden.» In this sentence, squash means what? | *A vegetable that grows on a vine | A sport with rackets | A crowded room | To press flat
test: Sam says, «It's a squash in here!» What does he mean? | It is very cold | *It is crowded | It is a sweet drink | It is a sport
exam: «He stood on the can to squash it flat.» Which meaning of squash fits this sentence? | *To press flat | A sweet drink | A vegetable | A sport with rackets
